  itemName: Canteen
  itemIcon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: a38cc2eca70368f4d9018bb5c0f0cd52, type: 3}
  description: A canteen of wood, tin, or glass to carry water was vital for a Militia
    soldier. The average for a march was between 8 and 13 miles per day and the capacity
    of the canteen was around 1.4 litres, this would have to last the man for an
    entire day unless they were lucky enough to find somewhere to refill it.
